(747313, 78466, 7322, '<td valign="top">Okay, now I recall. I liked this an awful lot but wanted a bit less blurring and yes, a less tight crop. You''ve achieved that and more with the second version. I''m so glad you continued with this idea. I gave this one a five, BTW. Pretty high for me in this challenge. :D</td>', 'Okay, now I recall. I liked this an awful lot but wanted a bit less blurring and yes, a less tight crop. You''ve achieved that and more with the second version. I''m so glad you continued with this idea. I gave this one a five, BTW. Pretty high for me in this challenge. :D', '2004-06-02 14:40:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(749204, 78720, 19504, '<td valign="top">I don''t get the pepper.  What does it have to do with the shot?</td>', 'I don''t get the pepper.  What does it have to do with the shot?', '2004-06-03 18:39:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(749379, 78856, 18080, '<td valign="top">I''m delighted to say that i called this shot wrong. I didn''t think it would do well, and it has... well done. I still love the irony of it.</td>', 'I''m delighted to say that i called this shot wrong. I didn''t think it would do well, and it has... well done. I still love the irony of it.', '2004-06-03 21:32:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(750000, 78680, 6999, '<td valign="top">Also browsing ... and for me by far the most interesting shot of the challenge. everyone else has resorted, it seems, to tricksy and slightly weird studies: you have found something interesting and dramatic, and genuinely photographic, in a true image of bananas. Top work.</td>', 'Also browsing ... and for me by far the most interesting shot of the challenge. everyone else has resorted, it seems, to tricksy and slightly weird studies: you have found something interesting and dramatic, and genuinely photographic, in a true image of bananas. Top work.', '2004-06-04 09:28:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(750141, 78564, 5728, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'Congrats on the well deserved ribbon!', '2004-06-04 11:54:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(750363, 78900, 16126, '<td valign="top">* From the Critique Club *<br/> <br/>The composition could have been interesting, but the tops of the bananas all lead my eye out of the picture instead of into it. Texture of the banana skins looks interesting, though the picture is too small to judge well. The B&amp;W works well with the overripened skins.<br/> <br/>Could have been a reasonably good picture, but the size really hurt it. Congrats on the brown ribbon, although I''m not sure you really deserved that.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-04 14:38:41.</i></td>', '* From the Critique Club * The composition could have been interesting, but the tops of the bananas all lead my eye out of the picture instead of into it. Texture of the banana skins looks interesting, though the picture is too small to judge well. The B&W works well with the overripened skins. Could have been a reasonably good picture, but the size really hurt it. Congrats on the brown ribbon, although I''m not sure you really deserved that.', '2004-06-04 15:36:51.000000', '2004-06-04 15:38:41.000000', 0),
(750367, 78701, 16126, '<td valign="top">* From the Critique Club *<br/> <br/>What most hurts this shot is the fact that it is out of focus, and it doesn''t look like you did that on purpose.  I assume it''s movement blur resulting from a slow shutter speed in a low-light situation, but I can''t really tell because you didn''t include the technical details.  Composition could be improved, the dark area in the top right corner is too empty, and the leaf obscures the bird without really adding interest.  If you had aimed the camera lower, you would have gotten rid of part of the empty area, and you would have had more of the bananas.<br/> <br/>Despite all this, the colors are great, especially the colormatch between the bird and the bananas. Keep up the good work!</td>', '* From the Critique Club * What most hurts this shot is the fact that it is out of focus, and it doesn''t look like you did that on purpose.  I assume it''s movement blur resulting from a slow shutter speed in a low-light situation, but I can''t really tell because you didn''t include the technical details.  Composition could be improved, the dark area in the top right corner is too empty, and the leaf obscures the bird without really adding interest.  If you had aimed the camera lower, you would have gotten rid of part of the empty area, and you would have had more of the bananas. Despite all this, the colors are great, especially the colormatch between the bird and the bananas. Keep up the good work!', '2004-06-04 15:46:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(750746, 78819, 14614, '<td valign="top">Hi Cole,<br/> <br/>Greetings from the Critique club...<br/> <br/>I like your play on words for the title.. it helps me know where you''re going with the shot and it adds a bit of interest to it.<br/> <br/>Technically the shot could use an edge(IMHO)-- much of it is oof although that could just be the slime on the bananas :)  They appear soft (no pun intended -- really) and for a more domino-like feel some thing must be crisper.  The bright light takes almost all the color away - it''s flat and so adds no interest by itself.  I like the diagonal line as it leads my eye through the shot.  The black background is just right to set off the fruit.<br/> <br/>I think you have a solid, albeit un-wow-factor shot.<br/> <br/>Hope this has been helpful.  PM me if you have any questions,<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Theresa</td>', 'Hi Cole, Greetings from the Critique club... I like your play on words for the title.. it helps me know where you''re going with the shot and it adds a bit of interest to it. Technically the shot could use an edge(IMHO)-- much of it is oof although that could just be the slime on the bananas :)  They appear soft (no pun intended -- really) and for a more domino-like feel some thing must be crisper.  The bright light takes almost all the color away - it''s flat and so adds no interest by itself.  I like the diagonal line as it leads my eye through the shot.  The black background is just right to set off the fruit. I think you have a solid, albeit un-wow-factor shot. Hope this has been helpful.  PM me if you have any questions, Regards,Theresa', '2004-06-04 22:19:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(750751, 78666, 14614, '<td valign="top">Hi Sally,<br/> <br/>Greetings from the Critique club...<br/> <br/>Congrats on the new camera -- more great shots to come I''m sure.  Nice result from your first entry with it.<br/> <br/>What stands out for me in your shot is your use of light.  The light and highlights on the cherries and apple are wonderful (over shadowing the banana which is the theme) and the red color dominates the shot.  This unfortuneately move the banana to, well, second banana (an expression in the states as the understudy but not the star)<br/> <br/>You''ve filled the frame with a pleasing composition so the overall effect is a lively still life/macro combo that works.  My suggestion for improvement: don''t have any solid ideas, perhaps a spritz of water, and a crisper apple.  This are minor as I, as well as many voters, liked this shot as presented.<br/> <br/>If you have any questions, pm me, please!<br/> <br/>Regards,<br/>Theresa</td>', 'Hi Sally, Greetings from the Critique club... Congrats on the new camera -- more great shots to come I''m sure.  Nice result from your first entry with it. What stands out for me in your shot is your use of light.  The light and highlights on the cherries and apple are wonderful (over shadowing the banana which is the theme) and the red color dominates the shot.  This unfortuneately move the banana to, well, second banana (an expression in the states as the understudy but not the star) You''ve filled the frame with a pleasing composition so the overall effect is a lively still life/macro combo that works.  My suggestion for improvement: don''t have any solid ideas, perhaps a spritz of water, and a crisper apple.  This are minor as I, as well as many voters, liked this shot as presented. If you have any questions, pm me, please! Regards,Theresa', '2004-06-04 22:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(751102, 78493, 19608, '<td valign="top">Hello Hans and <b>* Greetings from the Critique Club *</b> <br/> <br/>One of the indicators of a succesful image is whether or not it invokes emotion for the viewer.  As you probably noted from your comments - your image did so for most of the commenters.<br/> <br/>It was a very original idea - and although your technical aspects (exposure, focus, composition) were very well done, it still didn''t score very high.<br/> <br/>The question to ask are "What could be done to make it move up in the rankings?"<br/> <br/>I would suggest that you should do anything that would make it more "believable" - such as:<br/>a) Add a medical touch - something that would make it look more "hospital like" - instead of the wooden background.  Perhaps a miniature medical instrument - and a very sterile white background.<br/>b) Perhaps a "father" banana looking on.<br/>c) Mini receiving blanket in the scene.<br/> <br/>You get the idea - just that little extra thing that may make a voter who normally spends a few seconds... look a little longer before hitting the "4" key!<br/> <br/>Hope this helps - and congratulations on one of the most original ideas for bananas!<br/> <br/>-Tom-<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello Hans and * Greetings from the Critique Club *  One of the indicators of a succesful image is whether or not it invokes emotion for the viewer.  As you probably noted from your comments - your image did so for most of the commenters. It was a very original idea - and although your technical aspects (exposure, focus, composition) were very well done, it still didn''t score very high. The question to ask are "What could be done to make it move up in the rankings?" I would suggest that you should do anything that would make it more "believable" - such as:a) Add a medical touch - something that would make it look more "hospital like" - instead of the wooden background.  Perhaps a miniature medical instrument - and a very sterile white background.b) Perhaps a "father" banana looking on.c) Mini receiving blanket in the scene. You get the idea - just that little extra thing that may make a voter who normally spends a few seconds... look a little longer before hitting the "4" key! Hope this helps - and congratulations on one of the most original ideas for bananas! -Tom- ', '2004-06-05 01:56:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(751836, 78609, 20395, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Ah the silliness! I thought it was a cute idea- reminds me of one of those Richard Scary childrens books. I think the monkey has a car just like this! The main thing that turned me off about this picture was the color of the wheels and roll bar. I didn''t realize that you had used a different kind of banana- to me it just looked like they had gone bad under the studio lights, and thus were kind of icky. <br/> <br/>I know there is always some debate about the kind of pictures that we take on DPC- are they fine art, are they commerical, are they allowed to be utterly silly? I think that there is a place for all of these kinds of pictures, and I wouldn''t worry about the nay-sayers. <br/> <br/>Good luck in the future,<br/>Amanda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Ah the silliness! I thought it was a cute idea- reminds me of one of those Richard Scary childrens books. I think the monkey has a car just like this! The main thing that turned me off about this picture was the color of the wheels and roll bar. I didn''t realize that you had used a different kind of banana- to me it just looked like they had gone bad under the studio lights, and thus were kind of icky.  I know there is always some debate about the kind of pictures that we take on DPC- are they fine art, are they commerical, are they allowed to be utterly silly? I think that there is a place for all of these kinds of pictures, and I wouldn''t worry about the nay-sayers.  Good luck in the future,Amanda', '2004-06-05 22:28:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(751840, 78609, 19708, '<td valign="top">Hi Amanda,<br/> <br/>Me? Worry about the nay-sayers on a shot like this? It was done in pure fun, and put a smile on my face while shooting it. A grown man, making a car out of 100% banana - HA!<br/>One member thought the wheels were chocolate, so that would have been on the other end of the spectrum from "icky" I guess.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the feedback, and I hope I put a smile on your face when you saw the shot. If so, the shot was a success!<br/> <br/>Regards, <br/></td>', 'Hi Amanda, Me? Worry about the nay-sayers on a shot like this? It was done in pure fun, and put a smile on my face while shooting it. A grown man, making a car out of 100% banana - HA!One member thought the wheels were chocolate, so that would have been on the other end of the spectrum from "icky" I guess. Thanks for the feedback, and I hope I put a smile on your face when you saw the shot. If so, the shot was a success! Regards, ', '2004-06-05 22:40:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(760479, 78812, 12611, '<td valign="top">"banana hammock" is one of the best titles ever- and from a canadian! the phallic imagery is brilliant. freud would be proud!</td>', '"banana hammock" is one of the best titles ever- and from a canadian! the phallic imagery is brilliant. freud would be proud!', '2004-06-12 08:24:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(770199, 78665, 12042, '<td valign="top">Nei sko bara ísland. Ég kommentaði hana fyrstur en vissi ekki ða þú værir frá sama landi og ég og hvað þá frá sama bæ manni minn. Geggjuð mynd :D</td>', 'Nei sko bara ísland. Ég kommentaði hana fyrstur en vissi ekki ða þú værir frá sama landi og ég og hvað þá frá sama bæ manni minn. Geggjuð mynd :D', '2004-06-20 16:47:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(771204, 78910, 3765, '<td valign="top">A very balanced shot. Great colours and outstanding composition.</td>', 'A very balanced shot. Great colours and outstanding composition.', '2004-06-21 09:14:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(776040, 78720, 3524, '<td valign="top">Schoff, and anyone else who wondered about the red pepper...<br/> <br/>I had considered doing the shot without the pepper, but felt that for the perspective I was after, it needed something else to balance the shot in a few ways. <br/> <br/>1.) Color. The black background with the yellowish fruit had good contrast, but didn''t offer the brilliant splash of color I thought a circusy theme would need. <br/> <br/>2.) Odd number. I tend to believe that when there are distinct objects showing in a  composition, that an odd number is better than an even. That''s not always the case, but here, I really felt that the peel and the banana/melon combo needed a third party. So in comes the pepper. <br/> <br/>3.) Layout. The peel and banana-melon looked a little flat by themselves, and I thought the pepper helped add some punch and dynamics to the composition. <br/> <br/>If I had shot this on something other than a flat black background, I think that all 3 of these preceding reasons might not have been as big of a factor, since background items could have provided other compositional bits to satisfy me. <br/> <br/>Finally...4.) Story. Since my metephor was a human canonball, I thought that having The Great Banini fly through a hurtling ring of fire (or in the fruit world, a red bell pepper) would add to the ''daredevil'' part of the story.<br/> <br/>Of course, I know a lot of this is a matter of taste. And based on a couple of comments, that the red pepper was more distracting than interesting for some people''s taste. I think I still personally disagree with that, but I DO appreciate that people brought it up, because it did make me consider other ways I might handle the shot were I to do it again. Thanks again to everyone for all their thoughts!</td>', 'Schoff, and anyone else who wondered about the red pepper... I had considered doing the shot without the pepper, but felt that for the perspective I was after, it needed something else to balance the shot in a few ways.  1.) Color. The black background with the yellowish fruit had good contrast, but didn''t offer the brilliant splash of color I thought a circusy theme would need.  2.) Odd number. I tend to believe that when there are distinct objects showing in a  composition, that an odd number is better than an even. That''s not always the case, but here, I really felt that the peel and the banana/melon combo needed a third party. So in comes the pepper.  3.) Layout. The peel and banana-melon looked a little flat by themselves, and I thought the pepper helped add some punch and dynamics to the composition.  If I had shot this on something other than a flat black background, I think that all 3 of these preceding reasons might not have been as big of a factor, since background items could have provided other compositional bits to satisfy me.  Finally...4.) Story. Since my metephor was a human canonball, I thought that having The Great Banini fly through a hurtling ring of fire (or in the fruit world, a red bell pepper) would add to the ''daredevil'' part of the story. Of course, I know a lot of this is a matter of taste. And based on a couple of comments, that the red pepper was more distracting than interesting for some people''s taste. I think I still personally disagree with that, but I DO appreciate that people brought it up, because it did make me consider other ways I might handle the shot were I to do it again. Thanks again to everyone for all their thoughts!', '2004-06-23 13:26:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(839857, 78633, 8816, '<td valign="top">Deannda,<br/> <br/>This is a wonderful composition, and a brilliant idea, you definetly deserve the score you got!  However, with just a few finishing details, this could have broken the seven barrier and grabbed you a ribbon!<br/> <br/>As this was an ''advanced'' editing challenge, it would have been nice to see the background a true flat black, a little burning would have darkened up that right-hand corner which is slightly distracting.<br/> <br/>What type of lighting did you use?  The banana seems to be covered in a fair amount of shadow.  A good idea would''ve been to shoot this outside, as natural light would''ve given evenly distributed light across the entire photo, allowing us a fuller view of the banana.<br/> <br/>One technique that might''ve looked cool on this photo is selective desaturation.  If you had desaturated the face, it would have left only the lips and banana in color, which really would''ve given it a ''WOWZERS'' (which it already has, but even more so).  Also along these lines, it might''ve been nice to get rid of the red in the banana, which you probably could''ve done by using the sponge desaturation tool on the red channel.<br/> <br/>Those are my comments!  Don''t think I have all negative, cause I think this is a wonderful image, and am glad too see you placed so well with it.  Funnily enough, I took a picture very similar to this one for the freedom 2 challenge:<br/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=90111" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/234/thumb/90111.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/234/thumb/90111.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/234/thumb/90111.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>Good luck, and keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Lee<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-08-03 16:09:47.</i></td>', 'Deannda, This is a wonderful composition, and a brilliant idea, you definetly deserve the score you got!  However, with just a few finishing details, this could have broken the seven barrier and grabbed you a ribbon! As this was an ''advanced'' editing challenge, it would have been nice to see the background a true flat black, a little burning would have darkened up that right-hand corner which is slightly distracting. What type of lighting did you use?  The banana seems to be covered in a fair amount of shadow.  A good idea would''ve been to shoot this outside, as natural light would''ve given evenly distributed light across the entire photo, allowing us a fuller view of the banana. One technique that might''ve looked cool on this photo is selective desaturation.  If you had desaturated the face, it would have left only the lips and banana in color, which really would''ve given it a ''WOWZERS'' (which it already has, but even more so).  Also along these lines, it might''ve been nice to get rid of the red in the banana, which you probably could''ve done by using the sponge desaturation tool on the red channel. Those are my comments!  Don''t think I have all negative, cause I think this is a wonderful image, and am glad too see you placed so well with it.  Funnily enough, I took a picture very similar to this one for the freedom 2 challenge:   Good luck, and keep up the good work! Lee', '2004-08-03 17:08:26.000000', '2004-08-03 17:09:47.000000', 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
